cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Security - a nine-tool security toolkit in Python and Go
message: If you use this toolkit in your research or coursework, please cite it using this file.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Abolfazlrwm
    website: https://github.com/Abolfazlrwm
repository-code: https://github.com/Abolfazlrwm/Security
url: https://abolfazlrwm.github.io/Security/
abstract: >
  A compact toolkit of network reconnaissance, auditing and analysis tools -
  nine utilities in Python and Go with zero third-party dependencies, from
  subdomain discovery and port scanning to JWT auditing and CVE triage,
  wired together by a one-command reporting pipeline. Every tool ships as a
  standalone binary with build-provenance attestations and is exercised by
  unit and integration tests on every push.
keywords:
  - security
  - reconnaissance
  - pentest-tools
  - subdomain-enumeration
  - port-scanner
  - jwt
  - cve-lookup
  - directory-bruteforce
  - hash-cracking
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-23"
